# Double addition with integer operands

Adds 7 to a double in both operand orders to verify the integer is
promoted and the result stays a double, producing 9.25 when the integer
comes first and 8.5 when the double comes first.

>>> source
integer_left: int = 7
double_right: double = 2.25
double_left: double = 1.5

// Verifies the Int-to-Double promotion.
integer_plus_double: double = integer_left + double_right
print(integer_plus_double)

// Verifies the same promotion with the operand order reversed.
double_plus_integer: double = double_left + integer_left
print(double_plus_integer)

<<< stdout
9.25
8.5

<<< stderr
